  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. I didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **The discount was taken off after tax (`src/cart.js`).** `total()` added tax to the subtotal first and then took the discount off. The comment in the code and the tests both say the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal, so I swapped the order: discount first, then tax. For example, a $100 cart with a $20 discount and 10% tax now comes to $88 instead of $90.\n2. **A fixed discount could make the total negative (`src/discount.js`).** A fixed discount larger than the amount just subtracted, so a $5 cart with a $20 discount came to −$14.50. It now stops at zero (`Math.max(0, amount - discount.value)`).\n\nPercentage discounts gave the same result in either order, which is why only the two fixed-discount tests were failing.",
